{
  "homepageLead": "Welsh artist and creative technologist, based in Abertawe (Swansea). Working across moving image, sound, light, installation, performance and writing.",
  "writingIntro": "Writing moves through my work as stories, poems, performance texts and talks. Here are texts to read and recordings to return to.",
  "about": [
    "I’m a Welsh artist from Llanelli, based in Abertawe (Swansea). I make moving images, installations, performances, music and writing, and design light, sound and video for theatre.",
    "I’m interested in how images, sounds and objects shape our experience of a place, and how physical and digital acts of making affect one another. Those questions connect the clay figures and projected doubles of Y Cynfod, my solo performance what the fuck is going on? (or how I see things), and works that respond to the systems around us.",
    "My practice began in youth theatre and arts organising in Llanelli, before developing through community filmmaking and training in video design at Guildhall. I now work across independent projects and collaborations, bringing artistic decisions and the practical work of making them happen into the same process.",
    "Writing and performance are increasingly central to that work. I’m developing longer projects that bring image, sound, light, objects and language together, while continuing to collaborate with artists and theatre companies. I also share code, methods and documentation where practical."
  ],
